            <ArticleTitle>[Psychological aspects of relaparotomy].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>50-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors analyse the importance of the psychological barrier in the choice of the method of treatment in performing relaparotomy. Proceeding from the fact that the surgeon's psychological barrier is an objective factor aggravating the results of management of postoperative complications, the authors suggest that the indications for relaparotomy should be considered collectively. They believe that the second operation should be carried out by another, more experienced surgeon of the department. The surgeon who performed the first operation acts as an assistant during the relaparotomy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
